window.docContents[107].resolve({"/Environment/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Environment--Environment":{"contents":"Most functions in this library are in the Env monad, built on top of the EnvT monad transformer.\n\n#check EnvT\n\n\nBe careful that, in practice, EnvT works on monads that lift BaseIO so that it can call the\ncvc5 C++ API.Also for maintaining its state efficiently as a mutable reference.\nEnv is simply EnvT BaseIO.\n\n\n\nThe only way to run Env-code is through its run functions. The simplest one is Env.run and\nproduces a BaseIO (Res α) where Res is Except specialized to cvc.lean's Error type.\n\n#check Env.run\n\n\nCvc.Env.run {α : Type} (code : [inst : Ω] → Env α) : BaseIO (Res α)\n\n\nNotice that this function quantifies the Ω-instance inst for code. This guarantees that\nwhatever α is, it cannot mention inst in any way, so it is not possible for code to return,\nsay, an Srt-value as it would require inst to escape its scope.This design is heavily\ninspired by Lean's ST/ST.Ref.\n\nNow, to manipulate Env or virtually any type from the cvc.lean we need to have an Ω-instance in\nscope. We could have [Ω] as an argument of all our definitions, but it is often easier to have it\nas a variable.\n\nvariable [Ω]\n\n\nWe can now forget about Ω completely and write a few Srt-using Env functions:\n\ndef mkArrayBoolTo (srt : Srt) : Env Srt := do\n  srt.arrayFrom (← Srt.bool)\n\ndef codeInEnv : Env Unit := do\n  let real ← Srt.real\n  let array ← mkArrayBoolTo real\n  println! \"array sort := {array}\"\n\n\nNext we can use Env.run to actually run this code.\n\ndef test1 : IO Unit := do\n  match ← Env.run codeInEnv with\n  | .ok () => println! \"success\"\n  | .error e => println! \"an error occurred:\\n{e}\"\n\n#eval test1\n\n\narray sort := (Array Bool Real)\nsuccess\n\n\nRunning with Env.runIO lifts cvc.lean's errors to IO and makes this simple test much leaner.\n\n#eval Env.runIO codeInEnv\n\n\narray sort := (Array Bool Real)\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API\u0009Environment","header":"1.2. Environment","id":"/Environment/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Environment--Environment"}});